From b9b476c871b20ef4bc7622f58af5d14de2cfafda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:47:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/64] llama/CUDA: lagged conv history for the delta-net
 rollback by replay, no per-token conv snapshots (LLAMA_CONV_LAG)

With GATED_DELTA_NET_LAG the GDN state already lags behind the cell by its pending rows, but the conv state still
wrote a [d_conv - 1, nr] snapshot window per possible rollback (K = n_rs_seq + 1 windows). The fused SSM_CONV took at
most 8 of them, so drafts of 8+ tokens fell back to CONCAT + K CPYs + gather per layer (server verify 832 -> 1391
kernels at draft 8, 1585 at draft 12).

The conv cache row now holds the history around the pending rows of the last ubatch instead: rows t0 .. t0 + P + 2
of concat(history, x), channel fastest, where t0 is the first of its P <= K pending tokens. The history after keeping
n of them is time steps n .. n + 2 of the row, so a rollback is the same rs_pend_n -= r as for the GDN state, and
the graph reads it with a GET_ROWS of the time steps (rs_conv_idx input: n_keep + k, n_keep from the lag info) and
writes the new window with one transposed CPY. The fused SSM_CONV folds the gather and the CPY (strided windows
instead of snapshots), so 9-16 token verifies add no kernels; prompt ubatches run the unfused graph.

- ggml-cuda: ssm_conv fused src with strided state rows and destination windows; the cache plan matches the
  transposed gather of the history time steps and the transposed window CPY
- llama: llama_memory_recurrent rs_conv_lag (with rs_lag, single sequence), r_l row of (n_rs_seq + d_conv) time
  steps, seq_rm without the snapshot index, state save/load of the whole row; build_conv_state_lag
- test-backend-ops: SSM_CONV_LAG_CACHE_FUSION (n_t 1-17, K 5/9/16, n_keep 0/3/K)
- off-switch: LLAMA_CONV_LAG=0 (snapshots as before)

Server rocprofv3 (Qwen UD, MTP iq4_xs, 2 prompts x 256 tokens, T=0), verify kernels / verify wall / step wall:
  draft 7:  832 / 29.58 ms / 35.19 ms -> 832 / 29.51 / 35.08
  draft 8: 1391 / 34.17 ms / 40.79 ms -> 832 / 30.91 / 37.21  (cpy 428 x 0.89 ms, concat_non_cont 0.59, ssm_conv 0.17,
                                                              get_rows 0.10 ms gone)
  draft 12: 1585 / 36.36 ms / 45.67 ms -> 834 / 32.15 / 41.13
Greedy outputs (plain, MTP 4/8/12, both models, prompt-cache restore) md5-equal to d3a0973ae.
